on\":\"The admission felt like a release, a moment of pure honesty\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"After Nikki and Keith have sex and are lying together in bed, Nikki turns to him with her heart described as full and abruptly says the focal words. Keith pauses, smiles, and reciprocates.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"No specific undertaking is made by Nikki through the focal expression. Keith responds, “I love you too,” which accepts and reciprocates the avowal, but the supplied scene does not establish agreed relational obligations or definite future terms.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognise the work from the supplied text.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly presents Nikki's affection as genuine at this moment, but it does not settle the relationship's formal status, any concrete future commitments, or eventual durability.\"}"
